00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a United States Senator
from Vermont.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:05.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
Senator Bernie Sanders.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.673 size:78% position:39% line:92%
How are you, Senator?

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm great, Seth.
How are you?

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very well.
Last time we had you here

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.479 line:92%
was the day after inauguration

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:16.349
when you were the man who
launched a thousands memes

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I know you're a very
issue-oriented guy,

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.321 line:92%
and I do appreciate the time

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
talking to you
about those issues.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:27.027
But do you miss that your moment
of meme has died down a little

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:31.131
-Well, let me go into my pocke
and bring out my mittens here.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:34.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a bit warm, but --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
You know what?

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that's --
a lot of people,

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they had
their mitten moment,

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:39.839 line:92%
they continue to push it.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
They'd wear their mittens
into the summer.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you just let it go.
You moved on.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I moved on.
Now that it's 90 degrees

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
here in D.C., I said,
"What the hell?

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
No more mittens."
But you know...

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:53.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, I promise I'm gonna
talk about substantive issue

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
with you today,
but at the very end,

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do want to,
if you will indulge me,

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
ask about a few more memes
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But only when we're done
with the substance.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
Let's get to work.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
So, there's a lot of focus

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.502 size:84% position:42%
on how the early days
of the Biden presidency

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.404 size:81% position:41% line:92%
have been progressive.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the question
I have for you is,

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.975
do you think this is a permanent
move by the Democratic Party

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you think it is temporar
based on the crisis

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we have lived through
this past year?

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:26.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it is both,
but mostly your first point.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the President
and his staff are smart.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:35.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
And on issue after issue,
what they see

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that the American people,
and certainly people

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
who consider themselves
Democrats,

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.403 line:92%
support a progressive agenda

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:47.107
So, if you are a good politician
and you look out there and say

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.476 line:92%
"Hey, these ideas are popular.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:50.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
People who vote for me
support them.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.680 size:88% position:44%
You know what? Might be
a good idea to do them."

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.983
And the second point, though
Seth, is the question you raise,

00:01:56.983 --> 00:02:00.019
is the President -- I know thi
'cause I've talked to him --

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.956 size:81% position:41%
has also looked around
this world, right now,

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:06.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
and understands that, in terms
of democracy in America,

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether we remain
a democratic society,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we deal
with the terrible sufferin

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the working families
of our country,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.568 size:88% position:44% line:92%
who've been left behind,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether we deal
with climate change,

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:20.707 size:78% position:39%
that this is a moment
which requires bold,

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:23.576 size:84% position:42%
big thinking and not
the same old, same old.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I think that's where
the President is coming from

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:28.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It seems as though
the Republican Party

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:33.987 size:88% position:44%
has struggled in trying
to frame President Biden

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.156 line:92%
as this progressive firebrand.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're using
a lot of the attacks

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:41.928
they maybe had prepared for you,
had you been the nominee.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:45.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it interesting as you watch
them try to pin down a way

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
to criticize the Biden
presidency so far?

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:51.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is.
And the reason they're havin

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
a hard time is that, you know,
on almost every issue

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:01.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the President
is moving forward on,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
the American people and many
working-class Republicans

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.986 line:92%
support what we are doing.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:10.623
So if we say that, "In the midst
of an economic crisis,

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
which we are just
passing through now,

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're gonna put $2,000
in your pocket

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you may have
lost your job,

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:20.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're extending unemployment
or expanding healthcare,"

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know what?
Working-class Republicans,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.704 line:92%
not to mention Democrats, say,

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:28.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That's a good idea.
Thank you, Mr. President."

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One thing that we're noticing
and we've talked about

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
a fair amount on this show
is the Republican Party

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:39.686
continuing to choose to be close
to President Donald Trump

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:43.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
and their inability to move on
and certainly as evidenced

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.657 line:92%
by the fact that they vote

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
Liz Cheney
out of her leadership position

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:50.997
Now, you are not someone
who has much, if anything,

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:53.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
in common with Liz Cheney,
but are you surprised

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:58.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the speed in which the part
sort of kicked her aside?

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:02.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Seth, this is a huge issue.
I mean, it really is.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:07.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
In my view, I think
that the political debate

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:11.718
in Washington now is not about
healthcare or taxes or climate

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:15.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
It really is -- and I say this
without exaggeration --

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:20.393
it is whether or not we remain
a Democratic society ruled -

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:22.128 line:92%
governed by the rule of law.

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:25.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
What Liz Cheney's situatio
is about, as you've indicated,

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:28.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
she is a very,
very conservative Republican

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's a real
right-wing Republican.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.605 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But she made a mistake.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:35.208 size:84% position:42% line:92%
She actually understood

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:39.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Donald Trump lost
the election and Biden won

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:42.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said,
"We had fair election.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
Biden won.
Trump lost."

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:47.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for simply saying that
she was thrown out

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:51.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the leadership
of the Republican Party.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:54.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because the line is, you know,
whatever the line may be,

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:57.897 size:88% position:44%
is we are seeing a party
which is less of a party

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:02.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
and more of a cult
based around a big lie

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:07.006
that Trump won the election,
by the way, by a landslide

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when you go down that path
that there are Republicans

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have said exactly
what I'm saying,

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're going down the path
of authoritarianism

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:17.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
and undermining
our democratic society.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Very scary stuff.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:22.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Much has been made
of how it does seem as thoug

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.857
this is a party, when we tal
about the Republican Party

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
in disarray,
and yet you have warned,

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:30.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think that you are ver
cognizant of the fact

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.198 line:92%
that you cannot underestimat

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
the futures
of the Republican Party,

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:37.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just in 2024 but in 2022
in the midterm elections.

00:05:37.437 --> 00:05:42.475
How do you make sure that th
Democratic Party, at this point,

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:45.278 size:88% position:44%
understands that the --
you know, this is a very

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:49.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
temporary moment, possibly
insofar as leadership?

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's --
Look, I don't use the word

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:52.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
"disarray"
for the Republican Party.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:54.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
that they're in disarray.

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:57.223
I think what they are doin
and what their leadership

00:05:57.223 --> 00:06:00.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
is about is rallying aroun
Donald Trump,

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:05.264
who is a pathological liar
who is an authoritarian,

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:06.632 line:92%
who is a racist and a sexist

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:09.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
They see that
as the future of their party

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.104 size:75% position:38% line:92%
That's not disarray.

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:14.040 line:92%
That is where they choose to go.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.675 size:78% position:39%
And you're asking me,
"What's the antidote?

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you deal with that?
And it is not easy.

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:20.713 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It is not easy.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:24.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think one way we do it,
among many others,

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:26.719 line:92%
is to make sure that all people,

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:29.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
including working-class
Republicans,

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:33.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
understand that government
can work for them.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.495 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You don't have to, uh --

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
you don't have to be a racist.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:38.765 line:92%
You don't have to be a sexist.

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:42.034
That, in fact, government
can respond to your needs.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's why we are working
so hard right now on creatin

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:49.175
millions of good-paying jobs
rebuilding our infrastructure,

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:53.346
roads and bridges, expanding
that to include education.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're
a working-class Republican

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you don't like Democrats
but suddenly you see

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:01.821
that your kid can now get
a good-quality education

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
at a cost you can afford,
you know what?

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're gonna say,
"Thank you, Democrats."

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:06.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you see
that you have healthcare

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:10.963
when you previously did not,
if your minimum wage goes up

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:15.802
if your community now has decent
water and bridges and roads,

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:18.371
you will, I think, begin t
understand that government

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:22.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
can work for all of us
and not just the few on top.

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:23.476 line:92%
-I have a lot more to ask you.

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:27.180
We'll be right back with mor
from Senator Bernie Sanders.

